  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Bhaskar S/O Dhanji Patil vs The State Of Maharashtra And Anr on 10 October, 2018 Author: T.V. Nalawade Bench: T.V. Nalawade, Vibha Kankanwadi 1 In The High Court At Bombay Appellate Side, Bench At Aurangabad 958 Criminal Application No. 699 Of 2016 Bhaskar S/O Dhanji Patil Versus The State Of Maharashtra And Anr ... Advocate for Applicant : Mr. B.R. Waram App for Respondent 1 : Mr. M.M. Nerlikar ... Coram :T.V. Nalawade And Smt. Vibha Kankanwadi, Jj. Dated : 10/10/2018. Order :",
    "facts": "2. The crime is registered on the basis of report given by Food Safety Officer on 2.6.2015. He has made allegations that on that day, his police station received information that at Mangrul, Tahsil Parola, Bhaskar Patil, present applicant was manufacturing milk by using artificial substance for selling the product as milk product and he was attempting to sell it as buffalo milk. He took action and visited the spot with panchas. In a room, he noticed that by using mixture, some white material was being created and there were empty polythene bags and also some packs in which milk was filled. Samples of this milk and also oil which was found there were taken. In all 540 ltrs. of milk was found there. As the material found there showed that he was manufacturing the milk for selling and he was using the substance like milk powder, soyadrop oil etc. and he was not having any licence, Bhaskar S/O Dhanji Patil vs The State Of Maharashtra And Anr on 10 October, 2018 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/152482155/ 1 report was given and the crime was registered for aforesaid offences. 3. There is report of food testing laboratory showing that milk fat noticed was 24.36%. There was skimmed milk powder detected when it is not permissible to mix the milk powder as per the standards. Similarly vegetable oil was detected when it is not permissible to mix vegetable oil. The report shows that the sample did not conform the standards of buffalo milk as laid down in Rule 2.4.1 of aforesaid Special Enactment. Soyabin oil was also sent to laboratory. 4. The material collected shows that the present applicant was manufacturing milk for selling it as buffalo milk by mixing aforesaid extraneous matters and he had no licence for selling milk. Thus, he was deceiving the public and he had adulterated the milk. 5. The grounds raised by the learned counsel for applicant are technical grounds. He submitted that after giving F.I.R., the Food Safety Officer filed private, case which is given number as 163/2015 and due to this circumstance, the F.I.R. and the case on F.I.R. needs to be [LEAKAGE_MASK] and [LEAKAGE_MASK]. He placed reliance on some observations made in the cases which are as under :- (i) Application u/s. 482 No.30590/2008 dt. 11.9.2011 [Suresh Kumar Gupta Vs. State of U.P.]",
    "arguments": "\"4] The learned counsel for the applicant mainly submitted that in view of the provisions of aforesaid Special Enactment the crime could not have been registered and the prosecution ought to have been launched by Food Safety Officer by filing complaint before the learned Judicial Magistrate [F.C.]. He also submitted that the provisions of Indian Penal Code mentioned above cannot be used as special enactment is made to take action when food article is involved in the matter. Bhaskar S/O Dhanji Patil vs The State Of Maharashtra And Anr on 10 October, 2018 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/152482155/ 2 5] There is no force in both the aforesaid submissions made for the applicant.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "\"4] The learned counsel for the applicant mainly submitted that in view of the provisions of aforesaid Special Enactment the crime could not have been registered and the prosecution ought to have been launched by Food Safety Officer by filing complaint before the learned Judicial Magistrate [F.C.]. He also submitted that the provisions of Indian Penal Code mentioned above cannot be used as special enactment is made to take action when food article is involved in the matter.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "Bhaskar S/O Dhanji Patil vs The State Of Maharashtra And Anr on 10 October, 2018 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/152482155/ 2 5] There is no force in both the aforesaid submissions made for the applicant."
  },
